  "titles": {
    "_tiers_note": "Insular Celtic (Gaelic) clanhold, ascending; English display titles over the Goidelic conlang co-titles. Built on ri (king) and tuath (petty kingdom): Ri Tuaithe (king of a tuath) principality, Ruiri (over-king) kingdom, Ard-ri (high king) empire over the Ard-rige. Aire (noble) barony; Maor (warden) march; Toisech (sept-chief) county; Flaith (lord) duchy. A clan culture rarely rises past the ri-tuaithe. The brithem (judge) and fili (poet-seer) stand outside the ladder. (Native rank titles are the real Gaelic register, allowed.)",
    "display_policy": "Ruler/domain titles shown in setting-gen, domain lists and vassal trees are ENGLISH. The *_native conlang forms (Goidelic) are for NPC DIALOGUE ONLY, never for structural/UI displays.",
    "female_forms_display": {
